</p>
<br>
<p>Crude death rate \((CDR)=\displaystyle \frac{N}{P} \times 1000\) where \(N\) is the number of deaths and \(P\) is the population</p>
<p>a). Crude death rate \((CDR)\) for town \(A=\displaystyle \frac{{@sum_death_a@}}{{@sum_popn_a@}} \times 1000={@cdr_A@}\) </p>
<p>b). Crude death rate \((CDR)\) for town \(B=\displaystyle \frac{{@sum_death_b@}}{{@sum_popn_b@}} \times 1000={@cdr_B@}\)</p>
<p>To Determine Standardized death rate of the town \(A\) and \(B\) taking population of town \(A\) as standard population:</p>
<p>c). Standardized death rate (for town \(A\)) taking population of town \(A\) as standard population (this yields the same result as part (a) ):</p>
<p>\(=\displaystyle \frac{({@popn1a@}\times {@rate_1a@})+({@popn2a@}\times {@rate_2a@})+({@popn3a@}\times {@rate_3a@})+({@popn4a@}\times {@rate_4a@})+({@popn5a@}\times {@rate_5a@})}{{@popn1a@}+{@popn2a@}+{@popn3a@}+{@popn4a@}+{@popn5a@}}={@std_rate_A@}\) </p>
<p>d). Standardized death rate (for town \(B)\) taking population of town \(A\) as standard population (here we need to multiply the respective death rates of town \(B\) with the population of town \(A\) in each group):</p>
<p>\(=\displaystyle \frac{({@popn1a@}\times {@rate_1b@})+({@popn2a@}\times {@rate_2a@})+({@popn3a@}\times {@rate_3b@})+({@popn4a@}\times {@rate_4b@})+({@popn5a@}\times {@rate_5b@})}{{@popn1a@}+{@popn2a@}+{@popn3a@}+{@popn4a@}+{@popn5a@}}={@std_rate_B@}\) </p>]]></text>
